    "seo": {
      "title": "Iran's Cement Industry: Production, Clinker and Environmental Challenges",
      "description": "Explore Iranian cement production, the distinction between cement and clinker, and the evidence needed to assess industrial and environmental performance."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "industrial-context",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A construction material with a separate industrial geography",
        "content": "Iran's cement industry serves domestic building activity and export markets. The US Geological Survey identifies Iraq, Kuwait and Afghanistan among destinations for Iranian cement and clinker. These are related products, but their production and trade figures should remain separate: clinker is an intermediate material, while finished cement results from further grinding and blending. [s1](https://www.usgs.gov/centers/national-minerals-information-center/iran) [s2](https://www.iso.org/obp/ui?_escaped_fragment_=iso:std:iso:19694:-3:ed-1:v1:en)\n\nThis distinction matters when reading industry announcements. A clinker shipment represents a different processing stage from a cement shipment. Combining their tonnages without specifying the measure can obscure what factories actually manufacture and sell.",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "manufacturing",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "From raw materials to cement",
        "content": "The International Organization for Standardization describes cement manufacture as raw-material and fuel preparation, clinker production through high-temperature processing, and the grinding and blending of clinker with other constituents. Its process inventory includes gypsum, limestone, slag and other materials as possible inputs at the cement-grinding stage; the combination depends on the product. [s2](https://www.iso.org/obp/ui?_escaped_fragment_=iso:std:iso:19694:-3:ed-1:v1:en)\n\nA useful assessment therefore asks where an operation sits in this chain. Kiln production and cement grinding have different inputs and emissions boundaries. An increase in finished cement cannot, by itself, establish an equivalent increase in domestic clinker production.",
        "source_ids": ["s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "manufacturing-diagram",
        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "The principal cement manufacturing stages",
        "content": "```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Raw materials\"] -->|\"Preparation\"| B[\"Prepared raw material\"]\n  B -->|\"High-temperature processing\"| C[\"Clinker\"]\n  D[\"Other cement constituents\"] -->|\"Blending input\"| E[\"Grinding and blending\"]\n  C -->|\"Intermediate material\"| E\n  E -->|\"Finished product\"| F[\"Cement\"]\n```",
        "summary": "Arrows describe material processing. This generic manufacturing sequence does not document the equipment or product mix of any particular Iranian factory.",
        "as_of_date": null,
        "source_ids": ["s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "production-chart",
        "type": "chart",
        "content": {
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Iran: hydraulic cement production, 2020–2024",
          "dataset_id": "hydraulic-cement-output",
