          "y_axis_min": 0,
          "show_legend": false,
          "connect_nulls": false,
          "interpretation": "Output fell in 2021, recovered through 2023 and declined slightly in 2024. These observations do not establish the causes of the changes."
        },
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "environment",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Why energy efficiency is only part of the emissions question",
        "content": "Cement's direct carbon emissions have two distinct origins: fuel combustion and the chemical decomposition of carbonate raw materials during calcination. Electricity generation and transport can add emissions outside those direct process boundaries. Improving energy supply therefore addresses only part of the manufacturing footprint. [s2](https://www.iso.org/obp/ui?_escaped_fragment_=iso:std:iso:19694:-3:ed-1:v1:en)\n\nIRENA identifies reducing clinker use and changing energy inputs among approaches to cement decarbonization. These are technological pathways, not evidence that Iranian producers have implemented them at a documented scale. [s3](https://www.irena.org/Decarbonising-hard-to-abate-sectors-with-renewables-Enablers-and-recommendations/Industry-sector/Cement)\n\nThe practical conclusion is to read production, trade and environmental performance together, while keeping their definitions separate. National output establishes industrial scale; it does not establish plant efficiency, product quality or environmental compliance.",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3"]
      }
    ],
